       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is exactly twice the FDA maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. A single 1700 mg dose is also well above usual single doses, which are 500\u20131000 mg. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release. It may be what you meant if 1700 was a typo.\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** For example, 500 mg or 1000 mg PO two or three times daily, within the 2,550 mg/day limit.\n\nIf you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
