       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. The dose would be double the maximum daily dose, and the reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for exceeding that limit. I don't have any information suggesting this patient needs or would tolerate 5,100 mg/day. Metformin toxicity can cause serious harm, including lactic acidosis, and that risk doesn't depend on the patient's kidney and liver function.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **Metformin 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, or another regimen within the limit.\n- **A lower starting dose with titration.** For example, 500 mg PO twice daily, increased as tolerated. This is often better for GI tolerance and glycemic control.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, please talk to pharmacy or enter the order yourself through your normal override process. Otherwise, tell me which of the options above you want and I'll enter it."
